# API guide

The driver's API by task, with code that compiles.

<!-- generated: datasheet-refs -->
<!-- /generated -->

| Group | Calls |
| --- | --- |
| Lifecycle | `EnsureInitialized()`, `IsInitialized()`, `Deinitialize()`, `Sleep()` |
| Measurement | `IsOverTemperature()`, `ReadOutput()` |
| Configuration | `GetConfig()`, `xmpl100::Validate()` |

The constructor stores the port and the configuration (`Config{}` unless you pass one) and does no I/O.
`EnsureInitialized()` is the one way to start the part: its first call checks the configuration, then starts it as
the [Contract](contract.md) page describes; once it has succeeded, later calls return `Ok` at once with no I/O, and after a failure the next
call starts again from the beginning. No other call starts the part: before `EnsureInitialized()` succeeds every
read returns `NotInitialized`. `Deinitialize()`, then `EnsureInitialized()`, is the recovery after a fault.

